From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Render the device-specific settings with Compose

The 0003 migration left DeviceSpecificSettingsFragment on the View path
because its preference tree is built at runtime and it uses inline seek bars.
Finish that migration:

- let the Compose settings model discover screens at any depth, including under
  categories, and rebuild that index for each model read so pages added before
  the next read are visible;
- render SeekBarPreference as an inline Material 3 Expressive slider that
  respects the preference's adjustable range, is labelled for accessibility and
  writes back through the live preference when the drag ends;
- stop opting the device-specific settings out of the Compose host.

Dialogs, intents, drag-sort lists, subtitle lists with custom values and other
custom widgets still go through Preference.performClick(), so their existing
listeners, validation and dependencies stay in charge.
